 cid←{cid}MySQLConnect cfg;host;port;db;user;pw;cs;r
⍝ Connect to MySQL from APL using SQAPL (Dyalog's ODBC interface).
⍝ Needs the MariaDB ODBC driver: run Dyalog in the dyalog-mysql image
⍝ (see integrations/mysql/apl/README.md).
⍝
⍝   cfg ← host port database user password   (database may be '')
⍝   cid ← optional connection name; returned as the result. Without one, a
⍝         unique name is generated. Passing a name that's already connected
⍝         closes that connection first.
⍝
⍝   db←MySQLConnect 'host.containers.internal' 3307 'apl_demo' 'root' 'secret'
⍝
⍝ From inside a container, your Mac is 'host.containers.internal' (Podman)
⍝ or 'host.docker.internal' (Docker).

 (host port db user pw)←cfg

 :If 0=⎕NC'#.SQA'                     ⍝ load SQAPL once, into the root
     'SQA'#.⎕CY'sqapl'
 :EndIf
 r←#.SQA.Init''
 :If 0≠⊃r ⋄ ('SQAPL init failed: ',⍕2⊃r)⎕SIGNAL 11 ⋄ :EndIf

 :If 0=⎕NC'cid'
     cid←'MYSQL',⍕100000+?899999      ⍝ unique: never closes another connection
 :Else
     {}#.SQA.Close cid                ⍝ named: replace that connection
 :EndIf
 ⍝ {…} around the password lets it contain ; and other special characters
 cs←'DRIVER={MariaDB Unicode};SERVER=',host,';PORT=',(⍕port)
 cs,←(0<≢db)/';DATABASE=',db         ⍝ database '' → connect without one
 cs,←';UID=',user,';PWD={',pw,'}'
 r←#.SQA.Connect cid'' '' ''cs
 :If 0≠⊃r
     ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 11)('Message'('MySQLConnect: ',⍕3⊃r))
 :EndIf
